From: Ely Office
Subject: LOK: Impress sets a slide's title or body text by index

- .uno:ElySlideText (Slide, Box, Text) replaces slide Slide's title or
  body placeholder text (a title slide's subtitle counts as its body),
  one paragraph per line, in one undo step, without switching the shown
  slide. Empty text clears it back to the placeholder. A box whose text
  mixes looks is refused, as the notes are; one look is kept.
- .uno:ElySlides adds each slide's notes text and, per title, body and
  notes placeholder there, whether its text mixes looks.

